# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Step 1 -- clean the published dataset into the modeling table (single-file edition).

Reads ``data/dataset_all.csv`` -- the exact 57-column export of
``extraction/NiMSR-Miner.py`` -- and nothing else, then writes the single
modeling input table ``ML/data_clean/prep_output/ni_model_primary.csv`` plus
its integrity certificate ``dataset_manifest.json`` (the training stage
refuses to run when the certificate is missing or the table hash changes).

Which rows enter the model (1,503 of 6,341) and how evidence-confirmed
duplicate representations fold into one row (73 groups -> 1,091 modeling
rows) is a fixed published decision that was established by the audited
source-review chain and is NOT derivable from the 57 extraction columns.
That selection therefore lives here as embedded literals bound to one exact
dataset hash (DATASET_SHA256).  If dataset_all.csv changes for any reason
this stage refuses to run: a changed dataset needs a re-established
selection, not silent reuse of the published one.

Equivalence: on the pinned dataset this script reproduces the published
1,091-row modeling table exactly on every analysis-relevant column
(features, target, Paper_ID, split keys, row order).  Divergence is limited
to provenance-id columns: record_id / original_row_sha256 are synthesized
from row positions (the hex audit ids are not part of the 57-column export;
the position crosswalk to the audited record ids is kept in the authors'
audit archive).

Usage:
    python ML/data_clean/data_clean.py [--source PATH] [--output DIR]
"""
